= Karl Radek

The Comintern's man for Germany: born in Lemberg, a brilliant journalist, a wit, and a conspirator who has been expelled from more parties than most men have joined. He speaks for Moscow, though not always for the same Moscow twice.

- @money
- @advice
- @root: Return to main

@money
title: Ask Radek for Money
subtitle: 3 funds. Moscow will expect to be heard.
unavailable-subtitle: [? if advisor_action_timer = 1 : Next advisor action in 1 month. ?][? if advisor_action_timer > 1 : Next advisor action in [+ advisor_action_timer +] months. ?]
choose-if: advisor_action_timer <= 0
on-arrival: advisor_action_timer = 5; last_advisor_action = 1; resources += 3; independence -= 6; luxemburgist_satisfaction -= 3

Radek produces the money with a joke about capitalist banks. He is also taking notes.

@advice
title: Take Radek's Advice
subtitle: [? if lock_moscow_orders = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] Moscow's authority quiets the quarrels, at a price.
unavailable-subtitle: [? if advisor_action_timer = 1 : Next advisor action in 1 month. ?][? if advisor_action_timer > 1 : Next advisor action in [+ advisor_action_timer +] months. ?][? if lock_moscow_orders = 2 : The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids taking orders from Moscow. ?]
choose-if: advisor_action_timer <= 0 and lock_moscow_orders < 2
on-arrival: {!
Q.advisor_action_timer = 4;
Q.last_advisor_action = 1;
if (Q.lock_moscow_orders == 1) {
    Q.unity -= 10;
    Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10;
}
Q.independence -= 4;
Q.unity += 5;
Q.world_revolution += 2;
Q.offensive_satisfaction += 3;
!}

Radek listens to every current, flatters each of them, and then tells the Zentrale what the Executive expects. The quarrelling stops, for a while.
